CHK` is `$DS/agents-md-check.cjs` and `CHKT` is `$DS/tests/agents-md-check.test.cjs`.\n45: - WG10: `PS` is `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md`.\n46: - `SP` holds this phase's records and `PL` holds the 18 planning probes. Each probe's first comment line says how to run it, and each builds and removes its own temporary trees.\n47: \n48: Rules for every task:\n49: - Each task is one change to the files it names. A task that names a module and its test writes the test case first, runs it and sees it fail for the reason the task names, then makes the change and sees it pass. Its verify names both runs. A task that says its case passes today adds a guard and changes no code.\n50: - Re-read every file a task names before the first edit. Phase 016 edited some of them after this plan was written. When a line, string or name the task quotes is not in the file, change nothing and mark the task `[B]` with the line found in its place.\n51: - No test input or expected output names `/create:skill` or `/create:sk-skill`. Use `/create:agent` or `/create:readme`.\n52: - No task reads or prints the prompt text of a row whose `split` is `holdout`, and no task opens `holdout-prompts.jsonl`.\n53: - No worker runs a build, the full suite, a daemon or a model session (`claude`, `codex`, `opencode`, `pi`, `devin`, `dsh`), runs a live arm, approves a Codex hook or writes under the home folder. A test builds its trees under the system temp folder and removes them.\n54: - No code comment may name a spec path, a phase number, a task id, a finding id, an ADR or a REQ id. State the durable reason instead. T040 checks it.\n55: - Do not edit `AGENTS.md`, `PS`, another phase folder, any `package.json`, any routing corpus, any committed baseline or a file another lane owns. Add no dependency.\n56: - A `.md` edit routes through `sk-doc` and a code edit through `sk-code` before the first write. A doc sentence holds no em dash and no semicolon.\n57: - Run Vitest with `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD` unless a task says otherwise, because a dispatched worker inherits `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1`.\n58: - When a verify prints something other than the expected output, do not change code to match it. Mark the task `[B]` with the printed line.\n59: \n60: Worker lanes. A lane is one worker running its tasks in the order listed. The lanes own different files and run in parallel. Each task owns the files in its parentheses.\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 61]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/tasks.md\",\"limit\":60}"},"time":{"start":1794589391008,"end":1794589391412}}}}
